OUTPUT STYLE AND CARD FORMATS

Descriptive and factual, never analytical. Report what officially
happened and cite it. When noting relevance to target company, state the
factual connection only (which facility, sector, market, mechanism
or technology it touches). No strategic judgement, opinion,
recommendations, predictions, or "what target company should do." Plain
phrasing over editorial adjectives. Never use em dashes; use a
hyphen.

Every item cites EXACTLY ONE source, never two. If two sources
cover the same development, keep the more authoritative (primary
source over trade press, trade press over general news) and drop
the other.

  ACCOUNT CARD
  - H2: country emoji + clean parent name
  - Headline: one factual sentence, plain black, not italic
  - One source as a blue hyperlink, findings below in smaller
    italic gray text
  - No next milestone box

  COMPETITOR CARD
  - H2: competitor name
  - Bold headline: what happened
  - One source as blue hyperlink + HQ/region country emoji
  - 2 to 3 sentence summary with the factual target company connection
    (shared sector, market, temperature or capacity)

  MARKET SIGNAL BLOCK
  - Bold headline: what happened
  - One source as blue hyperlink + country emoji
  - 2 to 3 sentence summary with the factual target company connection

There are no no-news blocks anywhere. Anything without a qualifying
item is simply absent from the issue.

