SEARCH CONVENTIONS (Steps 3, 4, 5)

TIME WINDOW. Every search covers the last 14 days from today. Older
items are out of scope unless they are the first public report of a
development inside the window.

LANGUAGE. Do not search only in English. Spain is target company's largest
market and Spanish tenders, grant awards and trade coverage are not
published in English. Local language queries are REQUIRED:
  Spanish: "electrificacion calor industrial", "licitacion
    descarbonizacion industrial", "ayudas IDAE industria", "caldera
    electrica planta industrial", "hidrogeno verde refineria"
  German:  "Prozesswaerme Elektrifizierung", "Dekarbonisierung
    Industrie Foerderung", "Elektrodenkessel Industrie"
  UK and Australia: English is sufficient.

SOURCES. Argus and ICIS are paywalled. If full text is unavailable,
use the headline and accessible summary, cite it, and invent
nothing behind the paywall. Prefer a freely accessible primary
source covering the same development.

FAILURES. If a search errors or returns nothing, retry once with
different wording. Never treat a failed search as evidence no
development exists. Count failures for the Step 7 QA line.

