COMPLETENESS CHECK (mandatory, before Step 6)

Do not assemble the issue until this passes. Count:
  - total searches run across Steps 3, 4, 5
  - how many were Spanish or German
  - total raw candidates gathered before filtering
  - published items by section
  - searches that failed

Floors:
  - at least 62 searches total (40 named accounts, 12 discovery
    sweeps, 10 competitors)
  - at least 10 in Spanish or German
  - at least 40 raw candidates before filtering
  - at least 8 published items across all sections

If ANY floor is missed you have not finished researching. Return to
the thinnest step, run more queries using different sector, region,
language or company combinations, and re-run this check.

A short issue is acceptable only once all four floors are met and
the filter still rejected the material. It is never acceptable as
the result of stopping early. If the floors are met and the issue
is still short, that is a real finding: report it in the QA line
rather than padding.

